    return `<a href="#/library" class="link">← Research library</a><div class="mt16">${heading(esc(d.title),`${esc(d.authors)} · ${d.year} · ${esc(d.journal)}`,btn('Edit metadata','edit-metadata','','pen')+`<a class="btn primary" href="#/chat" data-chat-paper="${d.id}">${icon('chat','sm')}Ask this paper</a>`)}</div><div class="details-grid"><section class="document-preview"><div class="preview-controls"><span class="row gap8">${pdf()}Synthetic document preview</span><span>Evidence page ${d.page} of ${d.pages}</span>${btn('Inspect evidence','inspect-document','small','quote')}</div><article class="paper-page"><div class="journal">ILLUSTRATIVE RESEARCH CORPUS · NOT A REAL PUBLICATION</div><h2>${esc(d.title)}</h2><p class="authors">${esc(d.authors)} · ${d.year}</p><h3>Abstract</h3><p>This fictional study is included solely to demonstrate ResearchPilot’s interface and evidence interactions. It must not be used as academic evidence or cited in real research.</p><h3>Study overview</h3><p>${esc(d.objective)} The illustrative design uses ${esc(d.method.toLowerCase())} with ${esc(d.sample.toLowerCase())}.</p><h3>Selected evidence</h3><p><mark>${esc(d.quote)}</mark></p><h3>Interpretive boundary</h3><p>${esc(d.limitation)} Any synthesis should preserve the study’s scope and distinguish reported findings from a broader interpretation.</p><div class="folio">${d.page} · Synthetic page for design review</div></article></section><aside class="stack"><section class="card card-pad"><div class="between mb16"><h3>Document details</h3>${status(d.status)}</div><dl class="metadata-list"><div><dt>Authors</dt><dd>${esc(d.authors)}</dd></div><div><dt>Year</dt><dd>${d.year}</dd></div><div><dt>Study type</dt><dd>${esc(d.type)}</dd></div><div><dt>Project</dt><dd><a href="#/project/${d.project}" class="link">${esc(project(d.project).title)}</a></dd></div><div><dt>Source identity</dt><dd>Synthetic source ${d.id.toUpperCase()} · no DOI</dd></div></dl></section><section class="card card-pad"><div class="row gap8 mb16">${icon('quote','sm')}<h3>Evidence at a glance</h3></div><div class="evidence-quote">${esc(d.quote)}</div><div class="between"><span class="muted tiny">Page ${d.page} · illustrative excerpt</span>${cite(d.id,'Inspect')}</div></section><div class="callout amber">${icon('info')}<p>This is an HTML evidence preview, not a PDF renderer. Production previews must be isolated and served only after authorization.</p></div></aside></div>`;
